  "title": "Shah-i-Zinda",
  "summary": "Shah-i-Zinda is a mausoleum complex just northeast of Samarkand with some two dozen mausoleums, small mosques and a large cemetery. The University of Washington Silk Road page says it holds fragments of early Islamic structures, but most surviving buildings date from about 1360 to the middle of the following century.",
